# Exact Sketch layout module route

The current shared host returns404 for the new client import /apps/sketch/layout.mjs. The finite HTTP test authenticates and fetches actual candidate188 client/core/layout bytes. After adding one exact static-map route, both groups pass with10 source files stable. Existing Host/Origin guards, GET-only serving, private server/test/lib modules, other application scopes and encoded paths are checked. No broader arbitrary-file route is added.

The first raw run has two failures: one genuine404 and a test premise failure because Node fetch ignored an overridden Host header. Replacing that one probe with node:http leaves the baseline one-pass/one-fail; only server.mjs changes before the final two-pass run. All raw runs/source bytes remain. Six owned in-process HTTP servers use unique temporary stores and close after tests; no whole original app, browser, benchmark or production change occurs. The actual-browser campaign uses its separately disclosed private-host route adaptation.
